# Pairs with ListedRestorable. Production before the fix of #5449: a member
# of a multi-tree backup set registered its catalog row as soon as it was
# captured, and the set's membership stamp re-wrote its sink manifest and
# registered the row again once every member was captured. In between, the
# member was an ordinary listed backup, so a retention pass could prune it;
# the stamp then listed it again over the artifact the pass had deleted.
MODULE: ListedRestorableStampReregisters
TARGET: ListedRestorable
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a set member is registered at capture and again by the stamp
PERTURBS: Register

--- FIND
          \* A set member: its row waits for the stamp.
          /\ UNCHANGED <<cat, pub>>
--- REPLACE
          \* MUTATION: the member is registered now, and again by the stamp.
          /\ cat' = cat \cup {cap[c].id}
          /\ pub' = pub \cup {cap[c].id}
--- END
